      "message": "On ARM it is as follows:\n\n```\n        panic(\"HYP panic:\\nPS:%08llx PC:%016llx ESR:%016llx\\nFAR:%016llx HPFAR:%016llx PAR:%016llx\\nVCPU:%016lx\\n\",\n              spsr, elr_virt, esr, far, hpfar, par, vcpu);\n```\n\ni.e. some (hyp-related) info is printed in the next lines _after_ this `Kernel panic - not syncing: HYP panic:` line.\n\nSo why don\u0027t we print our hyp panic message after this line, not before? Especially if we must have this `:` after `HYP panic`. (It is confusing if we have this colon and nothing in the log after it, right?)",
